---
// Three Column Info section (Task 3, Course PDP Chunk B2) — Figma desktop
// 675:9040 (file FX7PDNvhZwyozODaq8Q8i7, "Gait Foundations Course" frame
// 675:9036) / mobile 1116:14704 (the "Gait Foundations Course" instance
// under the professional-courses mobile section 1109:14374). Prop is
// `{ item }` (same shape as every other course section — CourseOverview,
// YoullStopAndInstead, ComparisonChart, YourInstructors, etc.), reading
// `item.pdp.threeColumn`.
//
// ---- Why this file is written the way it is (10th-finding prevention) ----
// Rolling this section library out across courses has already produced TEN
// separate cases of a shared component with per-course content baked into
// it (a hardcoded heading, a hardcoded CTA label, a hardcoded intro
// paragraph, a hardcoded course name in an <h2>, an unconditionally-
// rendered caption with nothing under it — see ComparisonChart.astro's own
// header comment for the CTA/heading history, and CourseDetails.astro's
// "Review fix wave" for the tier-caption case). FOUR more courses render
// THIS section in later tasks (Tasks 5-7 + one more), each expected to
// differ from Gait Foundations in every way the data allows — different
// column COUNT, different item count per column, maybe no CTA at all. So:
//   - Every string below (section heading, each column's own heading, every
//     list item, the CTA label/href) comes from `item.pdp.threeColumn` —
//     nothing course-specific is hardcoded here.
//   - Every guard below checks NON-EMPTINESS, not just presence. `[]` and
//     `{}` are both truthy in JS, so a naive `column.heading &&` or
//     `threeColumn.cta &&` would still let an empty array/object through
//     and render a wrapper/heading/button with nothing under it — the exact
//     bug class this file exists to not repeat. See Pdp.astro's own
//     registry-guard comment for the composer-level half of this same
//     discipline (`columns?.length > 0`, not just `columns`).
//
// `item.pdp.threeColumn` = `{ heading, columns: [{ heading, items:
// [string] }], cta?: { label, href } }` (this task's brief-mandated shape).
// Gait Foundations' own 3 columns hold 3/3/5 items respectively — item
// COUNT differs per column, so `columns` is a list of lists, never a fixed
// triple destructured by position.
//
// ---- Check icon (new asset) ----------------------------------------------
// Each list item is a check-icon + text row. The icon is a REAL Figma
// vector asset (node `I675:9040;202:908;202:897`, a 24x24 teal
// (`#047791`) stroked checkmark) — downloaded via `get_design_context`'s own
// asset URL and committed as `public/images/pdp/check.svg`, following this
// repo's existing nav/PLP icon convention (stroke-path SVG,
// `stroke="var(--stroke-0, <hex>)"`, no width/height baked in — see
// `public/images/nav/icon-cart.svg`/`icon-search.svg`). This is NOT a reuse
// of ComparisonChart.astro's `✓` text glyph: that glyph lives in a boolean-
// `values` branch neither of that component's two shipped comparison tables
// actually exercises (both render literal "Yes"/"No" TEXT instead, per that
// file's own header comment), so it appears nowhere in this codebase's
// built HTML — it's a dead branch, not an icon asset, and reusing a
// never-rendered text character for a REAL, always-rendered icon here would
// just be swapping one unverified assumption for another. The official
// brand icon library (`01_Assets\00_Icons\`) also has no check icon (just
// `QuickCart.svg`) — so this is a genuinely new asset, not a missed reuse.
//
// The icons are decorative: the list text sitting next to each one already
// carries the full meaning ("Pre-Recorded videos to ensure easy access
// anytime."), so each icon is `alt=""` + `aria-hidden="true"` with no
// visually-hidden "included"/"check" string — unlike ComparisonChart's own
// boolean-cell mark, where the bare ✓/✕ glyph in a table cell IS the cell's
// entire content (hence that component's paired sr-only "Included"/"Not
// included" span). Nothing here is a table cell standing in for a value;
// every icon has a plain-text sibling doing the actual communicating.
//
// ---- CTA -------------------------------------------------------------
// `cta` is OPTIONAL (guarded below on `label && href` both present, not just
// the object's presence) — the 3 other professional courses that render
// this section later may have no CTA button at all (Figma frame heights
// already vary a lot across the professional-courses mobile section, e.g.
// 1116:16472/1116:17402 vs Gait Foundations' own 1116:14704, consistent
// with a genuinely optional trailing element, not a fixed 3-part template).
// `isExternalHref` (`src/scripts/links.js`) is this repo's one shared
// internal/external link predicate (already used by ComparisonChart.astro's
// own CTA and CourseDetails.astro's enroll CTA) — reused here rather than a
// third copy of the same `/^https?:/` regex, so an internal `/courses/...`
// href (a future course upselling a sibling page, same shape as
// ComparisonChart's Sole-Switch-to-Sole-Switch-Pro precedent) won't wrongly
// get `target="_blank"`.
//
// ---- Tokens / literals -----------------------------------------------
// Section heading = --type-display (700/40px), an exact match to Figma's
// desktop binding (`var(--text-display)`); mobile's own pulled code shows
// the same token resolving to 32px, but this repo's tokens.css has one
// non-responsive --type-display — same "one token, no per-breakpoint
// override" precedent CourseOverview.astro's --type-h3 case and
// YourInstructors.astro's name/credential tokens already set. List item
// text = --type-body-sm (400/14px), an exact match at both breakpoints.
// CTA label = --type-button (500/20px), an exact match (Figma binds it to
// `var(--text-button)` on both frames), teal background = --color-teal, CTA
// text = --color-paper — same button recipe as CourseDetails.astro's enroll
// CTA / ComparisonChart.astro's CTA (`padding: var(--space-4) 20px` — the
// 20px horizontal figure is a repeat of the same literal those two already
// flag, this repo's --space scale has 16/24 on either side of it, no exact
// 20px step).
//
// Column sub-heading (e.g. "What to expect") is bold/20px in Figma's pulled
// code with NO token binding at all (raw `text-[20px]`, not
// `text-[length:var(--text-...)]`) — unlike FourColumn.astro's 700/16px
// blurb text (also untokenized in Figma), no DS token pairs 700 weight with
// exactly 20px either (`--type-nav-label` coincidentally matches 700/20px
// but is a nav-specific token; reusing it here for an unrelated PDP section
// would be a confusing name/purpose mismatch for the same reason
// FourColumn.astro declined to stretch onto a wrong-but-numerically-close
// token) — so this is a component-intrinsic literal, same allowance
// FourColumn's own header comment already takes.
//
// Root section gap: Figma's own frame shows a 96px gap between its 3 rows
// (heading / column row / CTA) at desktop, 48px at mobile — 96px exceeds
// this repo's largest --space step (--space-8, 64px), so it's a literal at
// desktop, same "literal OK if bigger than the scale" allowance
// Testimonial.astro's own 96px section padding already takes; mobile's 48px
// is an exact --space-7 match. The gap BETWEEN list items (20px) is also a
// literal — no --space step lands on 20 (the scale runs 16/24) — flagged
// here rather than rounded either direction. Neither pulled frame carries
// its own top/bottom section padding (both show only horizontal px- values)
// — Figma's page-level frame absorbs inter-section spacing there instead —
// so `padding-block: var(--space-7)` is added here as this component's own
// choice for consistent page rhythm, the same "component supplies its own
// vertical rhythm even where Figma's own frame doesn't" precedent
// CourseOverview.astro's header comment already documents for its own
// section (also `px-` only in Figma's pulled code).
//
// Desktop column row is `flex` (row) with `items-start`, each column
// `flex: 1 1 0` + `min-width: 0` (matches FourColumn.astro's card sizing
// idiom, needed so long unbroken item text can wrap instead of overflowing
// its column); mobile stacks the same column blocks in a plain column, full
// width. Desktop's centered heading gets a 761px literal max-width
// (measured off the frame, centers the display heading without letting it
// stretch edge-to-edge on wide viewports) — same "literal measured column
// width" idiom YoullStopAndInstead's 424px panels / Testimonial's 916px
// card already use.
import { isExternalHref } from '../../scripts/links.js';

const { item } = Astro.props;
const threeColumn = item.pdp?.threeColumn;
// Non-emptiness, not presence — see header comment. A `threeColumn` object
// with an empty `columns` array must render nothing, matching Pdp.astro's
// own registry guard for this type.
const columns = (threeColumn?.columns ?? []).filter((col) => col.items?.length > 0);
const cta = threeColumn?.cta;
const hasCta = Boolean(cta?.label && cta?.href);
const isExternal = hasCta ? isExternalHref(cta.href) : false;
---
{columns.length > 0 && (
  <section class="three-column-info" data-pdp-id={item.id}>
    <div class="three-column-info__inner">
      {threeColumn.heading && <h2 class="three-column-info__heading">{threeColumn.heading}</h2>}

      <div class="three-column-info__row">
        {columns.map((column) => (
          <div class="three-column-info__column">
            {column.heading && <p class="three-column-info__column-heading">{column.heading}</p>}
            <ul class="three-column-info__list">
              {column.items.map((text) => (
                <li class="three-column-info__item">
                  <img src="/images/pdp/check.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="24" height="24" loading="lazy" />
                  <span>{text}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      {hasCta && (
        <a
          class="three-column-info__cta"
          href={cta.href}
          {...(isExternal ? { target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer' } : {})}
        >
          {cta.label}
        </a>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
)}
<style>
  .three-column-info__inner {
    max-width: var(--container-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--space-5);
    padding-block: var(--space-7);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-7);
  }

  .three-column-info__heading {
    font: var(--type-display);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-align: center;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .three-column-info__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .three-column-info__column {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* 20px literal — see header comment (no --space step lands on 20; Figma's
     own pulled code shows this sub-heading unbound to any type token
     either). */
  .three-column-info__column-heading {
    font: 700 20px/1.3 var(--font-sans);
    color: var(--color-teal);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .three-column-info__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    /* 20px literal — see header comment. */
    gap: 20px;
    width: 100%;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .three-column-info__item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    width: 100%;
  }
  .three-column-info__item img {
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .three-column-info__item span {
    font: var(--type-body-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    flex: 1 1 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .three-column-info__cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: var(--color-teal);
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font: var(--type-button);
    /* 20px literal — see header comment (same figure CourseDetails' enroll
       CTA / ComparisonChart's CTA already flag). */
    padding: var(--space-4) 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-align: center;
    transition: transform var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-standard);
  }
  .three-column-info__cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .three-column-info__cta:hover {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  /* ---- Desktop (Figma 675:9040, ≥1024) --------------------------------- */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .three-column-info__inner {
      padding-inline: var(--space-7);
      /* 96px literal — see header comment (bigger than --space-8, the
         largest step in this repo's scale); matches Testimonial.astro's own
         96px precedent. */
      gap: 96px;
    }
    .three-column-info__heading {
      /* 761px literal — see header comment (measured off the 1200-wide
         desktop frame, centers the heading without full-bleed stretching). */
      max-width: 761px;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
    .three-column-info__row {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: var(--space-7);
    }
    .three-column-info__column {
      flex: 1 1 0;
      min-width: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
